-- Saiki Rechat plugin: Follower control (MODERATORS ONLY)
-- SOURCE file. Obfuscate it with Ker0 (like the main script), then upload the obfuscated result to GitHub
-- (folder = CONFIG.PLUGIN_BASE). The main script downloads it with game:HttpGet() and runs it with loadstring().
--
-- Hook it into the main script with TWO small edits:
--   1) CONFIG.PLUGIN_FILES  ->  add   Followers="<the file name you uploaded>",
--   2) next to plug(nil,"Auras",...)  add   plug(nil,"Followers",{file=CONFIG.PLUGIN_FILES.Followers})
--
-- What it does: a moderator-only button appears under the chat bubble. It opens a window with
--   * the follower ranking, 20 at a time ("Load next 20")
--   * a lookup box (user id or username) to open anybody's profile
--   * profile + stats of anyone, with a REMOVE button on every follower
--   * auto-trim: bring someone's followers down to a number you type
-- REMOVE deletes the whole connection: the follower leaves that person's follower list + count AND that person
-- leaves the follower's following list.
--
-- SECURITY NOTE: the "moderators only" check in this file hides/blocks the UI, but the real lock has to live in
-- the sxikiflowsys database rules (only moderator accounts may delete other people's follower rows).
